# Protected publication

- Filter publication before links, embeds, indexes, and output. Keep unpublished and cross-group note content out of protected bundles too.
- The public Vite graph imports locked shell components only. Compile transformed protected notes in a separate in-memory Vite build, then write ciphertext after the ordinary emitter clears its output directory.
- Give each group a fresh opaque token per build. Put the token, never the group name or password, in public shell URLs and authenticated payload IDs.
- Bridge Svelte and client-safe Kit modules through host-generated facade chunks. A protected blob import must use the host's Svelte instance. Reject server-only imports before sealing.
- Keep keys, decrypted code, and private attachment object URLs in browser memory. Revoke attachment URLs on lock. The browser needs `script-src blob:` to execute decrypted modules.
- Keep `svartz:protectionReady` closed until host builds, browser mounting, output scans, and group search/graph behavior are verified. A partial implementation must fail the build instead of publishing a broken locked route.
